cal/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/scripts/aggregate_comparison.py:17:STATUSES = (\"met\", \"partial\", \"unmet\", \"not-checked\", \"not-applicable\")\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/scripts/aggregate_comparison.py:21:VALUES = dict(zip(STATUSES, (\"yes\", \"no\", \"no\", None, None)))\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/scripts/aggregate_comparison.py:971:                                n_applicable=len(selected) - counts[\"not-applicable\"], **counts))\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/scripts/aggregate_comparison.py:1004:                        # from \"not supported\" must never reverse a judge's verdict.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/scripts/aggregate_comparison.py:1007:                        # the verdict even if the same paragraph separately says\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/scripts/aggregate_comparison.py:1075:            n_applicable=len(valid) - values[\"not-applicable\"],\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/scripts/aggregate_comparison.py:1284:                      \"are separate. Missing observations are not verdicts; replay success is not required.\"}\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/comparison-plan.md:10:- STAMPED: retain every item verdict, evidence and not-checked value.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/judge-prompt.md:45:Cite artifact paths and evidence for verdicts, retain `not-checked` where appropriate, and report scientific adequacy and supported findings separately.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/scripts/comparison_figures.py:148:    ax.set_xlabel(f\"Assigned workers per item (n={len(runs)}); missing assessments are not item verdicts\")\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-