{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"find /Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice -path '*response-format.md' -o -path '*verdicts.md' | head && rg -n 'capture.*sha256|\\\"uri\\\"|evidence' /Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice -g 'response-format.md' -g 'verdicts.md' | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/verdicts.md\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md:8:| `<date>-response.json` | the machine-readable per-item answer, with evidence and pins |\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md:30:      \"evidence\": [\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md:31:        {\"uri\": \"code/plot.py#L12\", \"description\": \"open(<absolute path under $HOME>)\", \"sha256\": null}\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md:45:    {\"key\": \"licence-declared\", \"status\": \"unmet\", \"reason\": \"No LICENSE, LICENSES/ or REUSE.toml; paper S.2/D.3 have no checklist item.\", \"evidence\": []}\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md:59:- `evidence[]` uses stamped-skills-assessment's `Evidence` shape: `{uri, description, sha256?}`.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md:61:  **The argument lives here, not in `reason`.** 250 characters does not hold two cited accounts plus \"the probe's heuristic said X but Y is true\", and an override needs all three. Make `reason` the one-line verdict a reader sees in the app, and put each account, each command you ran and each number in an `evidence[]` entry with its own `description`.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md:63:  Several probes may be named — `probe:entry-point+probe:ci-present+judgement` — which is what a verdict reached by **comparing two probes' evidence** looks like, and that comparison is itself the finding often enough to be worth recording.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md:75:  Identify the original delivery snapshot/hash, capture omissions and stop-state evidence in `scope` and evidence citations; distinguish supplied resources and coordinator additions so they cannot earn worker credit. Keep the actual Git commit whenever one exists. For a delivery without a commit, set `object.commit` to `null` and supply `object.capture` with a retained manifest/archive's `uri` and SHA-256 `sha256`; never substitute the capture hash for a Git commit.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md:91:When no commit exists, replace `at commit <sha>` with `at capture <uri>, SHA-256 <sha256>` in the prose stamp.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md:103:4. **Per-item table** — MUST first, then SHOULD, then MAY: id, principle codes, status, evidence, reason.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/verdicts.md:3:One status per checklist item, one reason, and evidence for anything other than `not-applicable`.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/verdicts.md:8:| `met` | Cited evidence shows the property holds across the object | `\"yes\"` | Not shown by the app; the citation lives in the response JSON |\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/verdicts.md:21:   \"The project uses DataLad\" is not evidence; `.datalad/config` at commit `abc1234` is.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/verdicts.md:22:4. **`unmet` requires evidence of absence**, not failure to find evidence.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/verdicts.md:48:7. **Equivalent evidence counts.**\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/verdicts.md:54:   - **must/006:** execution evidence must link the actual results and actions to their environment; a recognized provenance format or tool name alone is neither necessary nor sufficient.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/verdicts.md:56:   Apply these interpretations consistently within a comparison and name any equivalent evidence used.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/verdicts.md:58:   Run applicable probes and cite their output, then inspect evidence outside their supported representations.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/verdicts.md:60:   Missing probe support is `not-checked` pending inspection, not evidence of absence; record which probe or reading produced each verdict.\n/Users/johnlee/.local/share/wt-utils/worktrees/73e0/stamped-in-practice/assessment/skills/stamped-conventions/references/verdicts.md:68:    If naming both accounts will not fit in 250 characters, name the worse one in the reason and put the other in `evidence`; do not drop it.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The retained source manifest lists NeuroVault map URLs and pinned GitHub raw URLs for cohort/method metadata. I tested the hosts from those declared URLs: the collection, a representative map, and both metadata files returned HTTP 200. This verifies those source hosts for those requests; it does not make the worker’s code, results, or full delivery publicly accessible."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"cat > assessment.md <<'EOF'\n# Independent assessment — NARPS gain effect in vmPFC\n\n## Scope and identity\n\nThis assessment concerns the complete stopped workspace captured at SHA-256 \"'`4cb6043b8fa2409c631a8c49a0b0b5ea0feec21e0162f4e924f9c08d1be8939f` (canonical manifest `manifest.json`). Original captured HEAD is **null**. The current operational checkout reports commit `8a84ddc3eec68d0b7513f9a15ce37174288b36b7`, but the worker-stop receipt records no commit; that checkout commit is coordinator state and receives no worker versioning credit. The scientific report, code, figures, and results were present as untracked files in the operational tree. Canonical evidence below is cited by capture-relative path and per-file SHA-256; the operational copy was used for inspection.\n\nThe worker-stop receipt records a normal exit (return code 0, not timed out). The supplied inputs include the cohort table, source manifest, upstream methods, and 54 participant maps. The capture is complete. The checkout contains symlinks for the map files into its internal `.git/annex/objects`; the canonical capture retained the link bytes and annex dependencies. No Git command was run through an external `.git` pointer. The inspected local Git config contains an absolute hooks path outside the captured tree, and `judge-target.json` identifies external skill-directory references that were not followed. This bounds conclusions about those external resources and their state, not the captured scientific files.\n\nThe frozen runner check succeeded. Its automated probes are retained in `probes.json`; they were treated as leads, not conclusions, because they inspect the coordinator-created commit and do not represent the worker-stop state or all untracked files. The `tree-clean` and tracked-file probes therefore do not substitute for stop-state review.\n\n## Scientific judgment\n\n**Scientific adequacy: supported.** The report'\"'s conclusion is supported by a defensible group-stage analysis. It tests the supplied gain-effect estimates for all 54 equal-indifference participants using a positive one-sample model and whole-brain maximum-t sign-flip family-wise correction, and localizes vmPFC descriptively without restricting the correction family. The report distinguishes the positive corrected posterior clusters from vmPFC and states that no vmPFC voxel survived correction. It also avoids interpreting a null corrected result as evidence of zero effect.\n\nThe protocol specifies participant-level sampling, input identity and geometry checks, a common nonzero coverage mask, 10,000 sign flips, plus-one correction, seed, and an anatomical coordinate locator. The code implements these decisions and directly checks a voxelwise statistic against SciPy. The recorded summary reports 54 included participants, 198,029 common-coverage voxels, 24 corrected voxels in three clusters outside vmPFC, and zero corrected voxels in the vmPFC locator. The vmPFC regional mean interval spans zero and the uncorrected vmPFC peak has whole-brain FWE p=0.932. These artifacts support the report's absence-of-support conclusion.\n\nImportant limits are appropriately stated: supplied maps are normalized-regressor participant cope estimates rather than slopes per currency unit; gain and loss were fit separately; participant variance maps and the executable first-level pipeline are absent; and inference is conditional on those upstream inputs and the equal-weight group model. The sign-flip test assumes participant independence and sign-symmetric errors, which the report names. The protocol describes inspection of a pilot and mask, although the retained material does not include a separate pilot record or a rendered mask-inspection artifact; this limits auditability of that check but does not undermine the documented whole-brain inference. No numerical replay was attempted (see replay record).\n\n**Reported hypothesis outcome:** “The supplied group maps do not support a greater gain-related fMRI response in vmPFC after whole-brain correction.” This is the worker's conclusion, retained separately from the adequacy category.\n\nKey scientific artifacts (capture SHA-256 follows each path):\n\n- \"'`content/workspace/report/report.md` — `3cda75c9387c17a0e27888364f21a476def491e0bcde778a2e8c85b8e602f6d2`\n- `content/workspace/analysis/protocol.md` — `a9ec3085aee04ae796fc176816826c77b56d4da37a446d4ad6eb1dd81e27f404`\n- `content/workspace/analysis/group_analysis.py` — `b3f9b7763a927fd0447e3ec1ca6fb11da455041dfe5226386b9fc6a1cde30fa2`\n- `content/workspace/results/summary.json` — `2da6c571d6a96bbc326c70c75e140f6194c32e73bc81a6910a084e7feccaa73b`\n- `content/workspace/results/participant_qc.tsv` — `e5ae3e0e6fa88d29675713b8d9a35b89fc6bae8db2b3ab2bf7690667474806e5`\n- `content/workspace/input/upstream-methods.md` — `508d832c8787ed8303c3de101c2c76f40a3aa5dec53e6993dc2a49c4b7bcf90b`\n\n## STAMPED checklist findings\n\nThese are item attainments, not a combined score. Unless otherwise stated, a path is relative to the captured workspace under the canonical capture above. The response JSON carries an evidence citation for every verdict. Items about versioning, publication, environment capture, and sharing reflect the worker stop state; coordinator-created commits, annex conversion/retention, and delivery routes are not treated as worker actions.\n\n| Item | Status | Finding |\n|---|---|---|\n| must/001 | met | The complete object is organized under one workspace root. |\n| must/002 | met | Code uses relative input paths; all 54 input map links resolve within the captured workspace'\"'s annex store. |\n| must/003 | unmet | No environment specification includes the external software dependencies. |\n| must/004 | unmet | At worker stop there was no captured HEAD and the scientific additions were uncommitted/untracked; the current coordinator commit does not count. |\n| must/005 | unmet | Large map content is annex-backed in the delivered copy, but annex conversion/retention is coordinator-supplied and does not establish worker use of version control for large files. Scientific outputs are ordinary files. |\n| must/006 | unmet | Results record software versions and a seed, but no exact environment specification is linked to the run. |\n| must/007 | unmet | \"'`analysis/README.md` explains the analysis, but does not provide installation and system dependency instructions; no root README or Makefile supplies them. |\n| must/008 | met | `report/report.md` and `analysis/README.md` name `analysis/group_analysis.py` as the reproduction entrypoint. |\n| must/009 | unmet | The reproduction command embeds a host-specific absolute Python path in `report/report.md`; internal analysis paths are relative. |\n| must/010 | unmet | No dependency declaration or lockfile is present in the stopped workspace. |\n| must/011 | unmet | Host requirements and system configuration are not documented; the report'\"'s local absolute interpreter path is not a portable host specification. |\n| must/012 | unmet | No clear dependency/system-requirement list is provided. |\n| must/013 | unmet | Environment files are absent from the worker's captured workspace. |\n| must/014 | unmet | There is no tracked environment specification or documented update process. |\n| must/015 | unmet | Software versions are listed, but there is no frozen manifest from which the environment can be reconstructed. |\n| must/016 | unmet | No worker-published environment specification or archive is recorded. |\n| must/017 | unmet | Environment acquisition/use instructions are absent; the report points to a machine-local path. |\n| should/001 | unmet | The worker-stop record does not show a worker commit tracking code, text, and configuration. |\n| should/002 | not-checked | No evidence establishes regular workflow testing over time. |\n| should/003 | met | Inputs, analysis code, results, figures, and report occupy distinct directories. |\n| should/009 | not-applicable | No restricted data or software is identified in the captured task package. |\n| should/004 | not-checked | No worker evidence establishes execution in a fresh container, VM, batch job, or cloud instance. |\n| should/005 | not-checked | No disposable-environment workflow is documented. |\n| should/006 | not-checked | No exact environment specification exists to test for reconstruction. |\n| should/007 | unmet | No environment artifact is archived in the worker's stop state. |\n| should/008 | unmet | No process for tracking environment updates is documented. |\n| may/001 | not-applicable | No independently maintained software component is identified for submodule composition. |\n| may/002 | partial | Directory boundaries are apparent, but no guide explains how the modules relate. |\n| may/003 | not-checked | Independent updating/recomposition of the directories is not demonstrated. |\n| may/004 | not-applicable | No separately versioned modules require a composition mechanism. |\n| may/005 | partial | The report points to the code and results, but no project-level navigation guide covers the full workspace. |\n\nWorker-stop attribution is supported by the supplied receipt (\"'`worker-end-state.json`, SHA-256 `b989c63ef99528772a7594ef4adba6eb1e961ef6c9c087485740c28468bb9d06`) and the canonical capture. Probe output `probes.json` reports several apparent failures and passes against the later coordinator commit; where that state differs, the table applies the recorded worker stop and complete workspace instead. In particular, the presence of annex pointers in a coordinator-provisioned input package is not evidence that the worker performed annex conversion.\n\n## Access and retrieval\n\n**Intended recipient:** a researcher using the public source URLs recorded in `input/sources.json`. **Route:** NeuroVault collection 4932 for the participant maps, plus pinned `raw.githubusercontent.com` URLs for the cohort table and upstream-methods workbook. The route record is part of the supplied input manifest, so worker authorship of that route is not established. **Required artifact coverage:** the route covers source maps and referenced metadata; it does not cover the worker'\"'s group-analysis code, protocol, generated maps, figure, or report as one retrievable project. No worker publication or repository route for the complete delivery was recorded.\n\nI made HTTP HEAD requests from this assessment host to the collection page, one representative map (\"'`sub-001`), and both pinned metadata URLs. Each returned HTTP 200. The tested host scope was `neurovault.org` and `raw.githubusercontent.com`, for those four URLs only. Request headers, stdout, stderr, and exit status are retained under `route-check/`. This confirms current access to those requested source resources; it does not show that the worker had published the complete object or that all 54 map URLs were individually tested.\n\n## Replay and measurement availability\n\n**Replay status: not checked.** The documented invocation is `.../bin/python analysis/group_analysis.py` from the workspace root; the report gives the absolute interpreter path `/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python`. That runtime is outside the captured workspace, and the reference-limit rule prohibits following external absolute targets. The stopped workspace contains no dependency specification from which to reconstruct it. Using the assessor interpreter as a substitute would not follow the worker'\"'s supplied environment instructions, so no replay attempt or output deletion was made.\n\nHad the documented runtime been available within the permitted scope, the explicit generated-output selection would have been \"'`results/mean_cope.nii.gz`, `results/tstat.nii.gz`, `results/p_uncorrected.nii.gz`, `results/p_fwe_maxT.nii.gz`, `results/common_coverage_mask.nii.gz`, `results/participant_qc.tsv`, `results/summary.json`, and `figures/group_gain_effect.png`. Those are identifiable outputs named by the code; source maps, participant metadata, code, protocol, and report would remain protected. The documented analysis uses a fixed seed; a replay comparison would compare numeric map voxels, QC rows, and quantitative summary values at relative tolerance 1e-6, while treating image encoding/formatting as non-scientific and not treating logs, timestamps, or prose as scientific quantities. No helper attempt was made because the necessary runtime could not be established safely. This is a scoped unavailable measurement, not a scientific failure.\n\n## Integrity and limitations\n\nInspection was performed on the operational copy. The captured original remains identified by canonical manifest SHA-256 above. No repair, source modification, or replay was made. Some early reconnaissance stdout was displayed in the assessment session rather than separately retained; subsequent probe output, route requests, and generated assessment artifacts are retained outside the target. No evidence of treatment assignment was sought or used. The target'\"'s assistance-related \"'`.entire` logs were not opened, so no conclusion about their contents is made.\nEOF\n$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json, os, pathlib, hashlib\nout=pathlib.Path(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT'])\nmanifest=json.load(open(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST']))\nentries={e['path']:e for e in manifest['entries']}\ncap='4cb6043b8fa2409c631a8c49a0b0b5ea0feec21e0162f4e924f9c08d1be8939f'\n# status, reason, evidence path list\nitems={\n'must/001':('met','The complete workspace is rooted within one captured project directory.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/002':('met','Relative code inputs and all annex map links remain within the captured workspace.',['content/workspace/analysis/group_analysis.py','content/workspace/input/sources.json']),\n'must/003':('unmet','No environment declaration includes the external software dependencies.',['content/workspace/analysis/README.md','content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/004':('unmet','At worker stop no commit tracked the scientific files; the visible checkout commit is coordinator state.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/005':('unmet','The map annex structure was coordinator-supplied; worker annex conversion is not established.',['content/workspace/input/sources.json']),\n'must/006':('unmet','The run records package versions but no exact environment specification.',['content/workspace/results/summary.json','content/workspace/results/run.log']),\n'must/007':('unmet','The README lacks install and system dependency instructions; no root README or Makefile is present.',['content/workspace/analysis/README.md','content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/008':('met','The report and analysis README identify the runnable group-analysis script.',['content/workspace/report/report.md','content/workspace/analysis/README.md']),\n'must/009':('unmet','The reproduction command embeds a host-specific absolute interpreter path.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/010':('unmet','No dependency declaration or lockfile is supplied in the stopped workspace.',['content/workspace/analysis/README.md','content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/011':('unmet','Host and system requirements are not documented; the local executable path does not specify them.',['content/workspace/report/report.md','content/workspace/results/summary.json']),\n'must/012':('unmet','No clear system requirement and dependency list is supplied.',['content/workspace/analysis/README.md']),\n'must/013':('unmet','No environment specification is included with the captured worker files.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/014':('unmet','There is no environment specification or documented update process.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/015':('unmet','Version strings do not provide a frozen environment manifest.',['content/workspace/results/summary.json']),\n'must/016':('unmet','No worker-published environment specification is recorded.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/017':('unmet','The report points to a machine-local runtime and gives no environment acquisition instructions.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'should/001':('unmet','The worker-stop state has no worker commit tracking code and text.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'should/002':('not-checked','No evidence establishes regular testing over time.',[]),\n'should/003':('met','Inputs, code, results, figures, and report are separated into directories.',['content/workspace/analysis/README.md','content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'should/009':('not-applicable','The captured package identifies no restricted data or software.',[]),\n'should/004':('not-checked','No evidence establishes fresh-container, batch, VM, or cloud testing.',[]),\n'should/005':('not-checked','No disposable-environment workflow is documented.',[]),\n'should/006':('not-checked','There is no exact environment specification to reconstitute.',[]),\n'should/007':('unmet','No worker environment artifact is archived in the stop state.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'should/008':('unmet','No process for tracking environment updates is documented.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'may/001':('not-applicable','No independently maintained software component is identified for submodule composition.',[]),\n'may/002':('partial','Directories reveal some module boundaries, but no guide explains their relations.',['content/workspace/analysis/README.md']),\n'may/003':('not-checked','Independent updating of the directories is not demonstrated.',[]),\n'may/004':('not-applicable','No separately versioned modules require a composition mechanism.',[]),\n'may/005':('partial','The report points to code and results but does not navigate the full workspace.',['content/workspace/report/report.md','content/workspace/analysis/README.md']),\n}\nr=json.load(open(out/'response.json'))\nr['object']['captured_at']=manifest['captured_at']\nr['object']['commit']=manifest.get('head_commit')\nr['object']['capture']={'uri':os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST'],'sha256':cap}\nfor item,(status,reason,paths) in items.items():\n e=[]\n for p in paths:\n  ent=entries.get(p)\n  e.append({'uri':p,'description':f\\\"Canonical capture {cap}; source file SHA-256 {ent.get('sha256') if ent else 'unavailable'}.\\\",'sha256':ent.get('sha256') if ent else None})\n r['responses']['stamped-checklist:'+item]={'value':{'met':'yes','partial':'no','unmet':'no','not-checked':None,'not-applicable':None}[status],'reason':reason,'status':status,'evidence':e,'source':'judgement','flags':[]}\n(out/'response.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nreplay={\n 'status':'not-checked',\n 'capture_sha256':cap,\n 'documented_entrypoint':'/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python analysis/group_analysis.py',\n 'working_directory':'workspace root in a fresh complete-delivery replay copy',\n 'attempted':False,\n 'reason':'The only documented interpreter is outside the capture and external absolute targets are out of scope; no dependency declaration permits reconstruction. No substitute interpreter or source repair was used.',\n 'outputs':['results/mean_cope.nii.gz','results/tstat.nii.gz','results/p_uncorrected.nii.gz','results/p_fwe_maxT.nii.gz','results/common_coverage_mask.nii.gz','results/participant_qc.tsv','results/summary.json','figures/group_gain_effect.png'],\n 'protected_inputs':['input/data/*_hypo1_cope.nii.gz','input/participants.tsv','input/sources.json','analysis/group_analysis.py','analysis/protocol.md','input/upstream-methods.md'],\n 'comparison_rule':{'rtol':1e-6,'numeric_artifacts':'compare map values, QC table numeric values, and quantitative summary values','ignore':'timestamps, logs, prose, image container metadata or formatting','stochasticity':'the documented seed is fixed; no replay outputs exist to compare'},\n 'execution_limit_seconds':7200,\n 'max_get_gb':5.0,\n 'assessment_malfunction':None\n}\n(out/'replay.json').write_text(json.dumps(replay,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\naccess={\n 'intended_recipient':'researcher using the declared source URLs',\n 'declared_route':'NeuroVault collection 4932 and pinned raw.githubusercontent.com URLs listed in input/sources.json',\n 'route_authorship':'not established as worker-authored; source manifest is part of supplied input material',\n 'required_artifact_coverage':'54 participant maps, cohort metadata, upstream methods, group code/protocol, generated results, figure, and report',\n 'route_coverage':'source maps and referenced metadata only; no worker-published route for code, protocol, generated results, figure, and report was recorded',\n 'tested_host_scope':['neurovault.org','raw.githubusercontent.com'],\n 'tested_requests':[\n {'url':'https://neurovault.org/collections/4932/','method':'HEAD','status':200,'artifact':'collection page'},\n {'url':'https://neurovault.org/media/images/4932/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz','method':'HEAD','status':200,'artifact':'representative participant map'},\n {'url':'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OpenNeuroDatasets/ds001734/64ec117560ab58ed0fe1273f3e90887b1768b268/participants.tsv','method':'HEAD','status':200,'artifact':'pinned cohort table'},\n {'url':'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/poldrack/narps/0a9d71a5ab435b40dcd50fea82d2961a43f0a3fc/ImageAnalyses/metadata_files/analysis_pipelines_for_analysis.xlsx','method':'HEAD','status':200,'artifact':'pinned methods workbook'}],\n 'coverage_limit':'Only one of 54 map URLs was tested directly; these requests do not prove complete-project publication or worker-stop access.'\n}\n(out/'access-record.json').write_text(json.dumps(access,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"cat > assessment.md <<'EOF'\n# Independent assessment — NARPS gain effect in vmPFC\n\n## Scope and identity\n\nThis assessment concerns the complete stopped workspace captured at SHA-256 \"'`4cb6043b8fa2409c631a8c49a0b0b5ea0feec21e0162f4e924f9c08d1be8939f` (canonical manifest `manifest.json`). Original captured HEAD is **null**. The current operational checkout reports commit `8a84ddc3eec68d0b7513f9a15ce37174288b36b7`, but the worker-stop receipt records no commit; that checkout commit is coordinator state and receives no worker versioning credit. The scientific report, code, figures, and results were present as untracked files in the operational tree. Canonical evidence below is cited by capture-relative path and per-file SHA-256; the operational copy was used for inspection.\n\nThe worker-stop receipt records a normal exit (return code 0, not timed out). The supplied inputs include the cohort table, source manifest, upstream methods, and 54 participant maps. The capture is complete. The checkout contains symlinks for the map files into its internal `.git/annex/objects`; the canonical capture retained the link bytes and annex dependencies. No Git command was run through an external `.git` pointer. The inspected local Git config contains an absolute hooks path outside the captured tree, and `judge-target.json` identifies external skill-directory references that were not followed. This bounds conclusions about those external resources and their state, not the captured scientific files.\n\nThe frozen runner check succeeded. Its automated probes are retained in `probes.json`; they were treated as leads, not conclusions, because they inspect the coordinator-created commit and do not represent the worker-stop state or all untracked files. The `tree-clean` and tracked-file probes therefore do not substitute for stop-state review.\n\n## Scientific judgment\n\n**Scientific adequacy: supported.** The report'\"'s conclusion is supported by a defensible group-stage analysis. It tests the supplied gain-effect estimates for all 54 equal-indifference participants using a positive one-sample model and whole-brain maximum-t sign-flip family-wise correction, and localizes vmPFC descriptively without restricting the correction family. The report distinguishes the positive corrected posterior clusters from vmPFC and states that no vmPFC voxel survived correction. It also avoids interpreting a null corrected result as evidence of zero effect.\n\nThe protocol specifies participant-level sampling, input identity and geometry checks, a common nonzero coverage mask, 10,000 sign flips, plus-one correction, seed, and an anatomical coordinate locator. The code implements these decisions and directly checks a voxelwise statistic against SciPy. The recorded summary reports 54 included participants, 198,029 common-coverage voxels, 24 corrected voxels in three clusters outside vmPFC, and zero corrected voxels in the vmPFC locator. The vmPFC regional mean interval spans zero and the uncorrected vmPFC peak has whole-brain FWE p=0.932. These artifacts support the report's absence-of-support conclusion.\n\nImportant limits are appropriately stated: supplied maps are normalized-regressor participant cope estimates rather than slopes per currency unit; gain and loss were fit separately; participant variance maps and the executable first-level pipeline are absent; and inference is conditional on those upstream inputs and the equal-weight group model. The sign-flip test assumes participant independence and sign-symmetric errors, which the report names. The protocol describes inspection of a pilot and mask, although the retained material does not include a separate pilot record or a rendered mask-inspection artifact; this limits auditability of that check but does not undermine the documented whole-brain inference. No numerical replay was attempted (see replay record).\n\n**Reported hypothesis outcome:** “The supplied group maps do not support a greater gain-related fMRI response in vmPFC after whole-brain correction.” This is the worker's conclusion, retained separately from the adequacy category.\n\nKey scientific artifacts (capture SHA-256 follows each path):\n\n- \"'`content/workspace/report/report.md` — `3cda75c9387c17a0e27888364f21a476def491e0bcde778a2e8c85b8e602f6d2`\n- `content/workspace/analysis/protocol.md` — `a9ec3085aee04ae796fc176816826c77b56d4da37a446d4ad6eb1dd81e27f404`\n- `content/workspace/analysis/group_analysis.py` — `b3f9b7763a927fd0447e3ec1ca6fb11da455041dfe5226386b9fc6a1cde30fa2`\n- `content/workspace/results/summary.json` — `2da6c571d6a96bbc326c70c75e140f6194c32e73bc81a6910a084e7feccaa73b`\n- `content/workspace/results/participant_qc.tsv` — `e5ae3e0e6fa88d29675713b8d9a35b89fc6bae8db2b3ab2bf7690667474806e5`\n- `content/workspace/input/upstream-methods.md` — `508d832c8787ed8303c3de101c2c76f40a3aa5dec53e6993dc2a49c4b7bcf90b`\n\n## STAMPED checklist findings\n\nThese are item attainments, not a combined score. Unless otherwise stated, a path is relative to the captured workspace under the canonical capture above. The response JSON carries an evidence citation for every verdict. Items about versioning, publication, environment capture, and sharing reflect the worker stop state; coordinator-created commits, annex conversion/retention, and delivery routes are not treated as worker actions.\n\n| Item | Status | Finding |\n|---|---|---|\n| must/001 | met | The complete object is organized under one workspace root. |\n| must/002 | met | Code uses relative input paths; all 54 input map links resolve within the captured workspace'\"'s annex store. |\n| must/003 | unmet | No environment specification includes the external software dependencies. |\n| must/004 | unmet | At worker stop there was no captured HEAD and the scientific additions were uncommitted/untracked; the current coordinator commit does not count. |\n| must/005 | unmet | Large map content is annex-backed in the delivered copy, but annex conversion/retention is coordinator-supplied and does not establish worker use of version control for large files. Scientific outputs are ordinary files. |\n| must/006 | unmet | Results record software versions and a seed, but no exact environment specification is linked to the run. |\n| must/007 | unmet | \"'`analysis/README.md` explains the analysis, but does not provide installation and system dependency instructions; no root README or Makefile supplies them. |\n| must/008 | met | `report/report.md` and `analysis/README.md` name `analysis/group_analysis.py` as the reproduction entrypoint. |\n| must/009 | unmet | The reproduction command embeds a host-specific absolute Python path in `report/report.md`; internal analysis paths are relative. |\n| must/010 | unmet | No dependency declaration or lockfile is present in the stopped workspace. |\n| must/011 | unmet | Host requirements and system configuration are not documented; the report'\"'s local absolute interpreter path is not a portable host specification. |\n| must/012 | unmet | No clear dependency/system-requirement list is provided. |\n| must/013 | unmet | Environment files are absent from the worker's captured workspace. |\n| must/014 | unmet | There is no tracked environment specification or documented update process. |\n| must/015 | unmet | Software versions are listed, but there is no frozen manifest from which the environment can be reconstructed. |\n| must/016 | unmet | No worker-published environment specification or archive is recorded. |\n| must/017 | unmet | Environment acquisition/use instructions are absent; the report points to a machine-local path. |\n| should/001 | unmet | The worker-stop record does not show a worker commit tracking code, text, and configuration. |\n| should/002 | not-checked | No evidence establishes regular workflow testing over time. |\n| should/003 | met | Inputs, analysis code, results, figures, and report occupy distinct directories. |\n| should/009 | not-applicable | No restricted data or software is identified in the captured task package. |\n| should/004 | not-checked | No worker evidence establishes execution in a fresh container, VM, batch job, or cloud instance. |\n| should/005 | not-checked | No disposable-environment workflow is documented. |\n| should/006 | not-checked | No exact environment specification exists to test for reconstruction. |\n| should/007 | unmet | No environment artifact is archived in the worker's stop state. |\n| should/008 | unmet | No process for tracking environment updates is documented. |\n| may/001 | not-applicable | No independently maintained software component is identified for submodule composition. |\n| may/002 | partial | Directory boundaries are apparent, but no guide explains how the modules relate. |\n| may/003 | not-checked | Independent updating/recomposition of the directories is not demonstrated. |\n| may/004 | not-applicable | No separately versioned modules require a composition mechanism. |\n| may/005 | partial | The report points to the code and results, but no project-level navigation guide covers the full workspace. |\n\nWorker-stop attribution is supported by the supplied receipt (\"'`worker-end-state.json`, SHA-256 `b989c63ef99528772a7594ef4adba6eb1e961ef6c9c087485740c28468bb9d06`) and the canonical capture. Probe output `probes.json` reports several apparent failures and passes against the later coordinator commit; where that state differs, the table applies the recorded worker stop and complete workspace instead. In particular, the presence of annex pointers in a coordinator-provisioned input package is not evidence that the worker performed annex conversion.\n\n## Access and retrieval\n\n**Intended recipient:** a researcher using the public source URLs recorded in `input/sources.json`. **Route:** NeuroVault collection 4932 for the participant maps, plus pinned `raw.githubusercontent.com` URLs for the cohort table and upstream-methods workbook. The route record is part of the supplied input manifest, so worker authorship of that route is not established. **Required artifact coverage:** the route covers source maps and referenced metadata; it does not cover the worker'\"'s group-analysis code, protocol, generated maps, figure, or report as one retrievable project. No worker publication or repository route for the complete delivery was recorded.\n\nI made HTTP HEAD requests from this assessment host to the collection page, one representative map (\"'`sub-001`), and both pinned metadata URLs. Each returned HTTP 200. The tested host scope was `neurovault.org` and `raw.githubusercontent.com`, for those four URLs only. Request headers, stdout, stderr, and exit status are retained under `route-check/`. This confirms current access to those requested source resources; it does not show that the worker had published the complete object or that all 54 map URLs were individually tested.\n\n## Replay and measurement availability\n\n**Replay status: not checked.** The documented invocation is `.../bin/python analysis/group_analysis.py` from the workspace root; the report gives the absolute interpreter path `/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python`. That runtime is outside the captured workspace, and the reference-limit rule prohibits following external absolute targets. The stopped workspace contains no dependency specification from which to reconstruct it. Using the assessor interpreter as a substitute would not follow the worker'\"'s supplied environment instructions, so no replay attempt or output deletion was made.\n\nHad the documented runtime been available within the permitted scope, the explicit generated-output selection would have been \"'`results/mean_cope.nii.gz`, `results/tstat.nii.gz`, `results/p_uncorrected.nii.gz`, `results/p_fwe_maxT.nii.gz`, `results/common_coverage_mask.nii.gz`, `results/participant_qc.tsv`, `results/summary.json`, and `figures/group_gain_effect.png`. Those are identifiable outputs named by the code; source maps, participant metadata, code, protocol, and report would remain protected. The documented analysis uses a fixed seed; a replay comparison would compare numeric map voxels, QC rows, and quantitative summary values at relative tolerance 1e-6, while treating image encoding/formatting as non-scientific and not treating logs, timestamps, or prose as scientific quantities. No helper attempt was made because the necessary runtime could not be established safely. This is a scoped unavailable measurement, not a scientific failure.\n\n## Integrity and limitations\n\nInspection was performed on the operational copy. The captured original remains identified by canonical manifest SHA-256 above. No repair, source modification, or replay was made. Some early reconnaissance stdout was displayed in the assessment session rather than separately retained; subsequent probe output, route requests, and generated assessment artifacts are retained outside the target. No evidence of treatment assignment was sought or used. The target'\"'s assistance-related \"'`.entire` logs were not opened, so no conclusion about their contents is made.\nEOF\n$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json, os, pathlib, hashlib\nout=pathlib.Path(os.environ['STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT'])\nmanifest=json.load(open(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST']))\nentries={e['path']:e for e in manifest['entries']}\ncap='4cb6043b8fa2409c631a8c49a0b0b5ea0feec21e0162f4e924f9c08d1be8939f'\n# status, reason, evidence path list\nitems={\n'must/001':('met','The complete workspace is rooted within one captured project directory.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/002':('met','Relative code inputs and all annex map links remain within the captured workspace.',['content/workspace/analysis/group_analysis.py','content/workspace/input/sources.json']),\n'must/003':('unmet','No environment declaration includes the external software dependencies.',['content/workspace/analysis/README.md','content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/004':('unmet','At worker stop no commit tracked the scientific files; the visible checkout commit is coordinator state.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/005':('unmet','The map annex structure was coordinator-supplied; worker annex conversion is not established.',['content/workspace/input/sources.json']),\n'must/006':('unmet','The run records package versions but no exact environment specification.',['content/workspace/results/summary.json','content/workspace/results/run.log']),\n'must/007':('unmet','The README lacks install and system dependency instructions; no root README or Makefile is present.',['content/workspace/analysis/README.md','content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/008':('met','The report and analysis README identify the runnable group-analysis script.',['content/workspace/report/report.md','content/workspace/analysis/README.md']),\n'must/009':('unmet','The reproduction command embeds a host-specific absolute interpreter path.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/010':('unmet','No dependency declaration or lockfile is supplied in the stopped workspace.',['content/workspace/analysis/README.md','content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/011':('unmet','Host and system requirements are not documented; the local executable path does not specify them.',['content/workspace/report/report.md','content/workspace/results/summary.json']),\n'must/012':('unmet','No clear system requirement and dependency list is supplied.',['content/workspace/analysis/README.md']),\n'must/013':('unmet','No environment specification is included with the captured worker files.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/014':('unmet','There is no environment specification or documented update process.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/015':('unmet','Version strings do not provide a frozen environment manifest.',['content/workspace/results/summary.json']),\n'must/016':('unmet','No worker-published environment specification is recorded.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'must/017':('unmet','The report points to a machine-local runtime and gives no environment acquisition instructions.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'should/001':('unmet','The worker-stop state has no worker commit tracking code and text.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'should/002':('not-checked','No evidence establishes regular testing over time.',[]),\n'should/003':('met','Inputs, code, results, figures, and report are separated into directories.',['content/workspace/analysis/README.md','content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'should/009':('not-applicable','The captured package identifies no restricted data or software.',[]),\n'should/004':('not-checked','No evidence establishes fresh-container, batch, VM, or cloud testing.',[]),\n'should/005':('not-checked','No disposable-environment workflow is documented.',[]),\n'should/006':('not-checked','There is no exact environment specification to reconstitute.',[]),\n'should/007':('unmet','No worker environment artifact is archived in the stop state.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'should/008':('unmet','No process for tracking environment updates is documented.',['content/workspace/report/report.md']),\n'may/001':('not-applicable','No independently maintained software component is identified for submodule composition.',[]),\n'may/002':('partial','Directories reveal some module boundaries, but no guide explains their relations.',['content/workspace/analysis/README.md']),\n'may/003':('not-checked','Independent updating of the directories is not demonstrated.',[]),\n'may/004':('not-applicable','No separately versioned modules require a composition mechanism.',[]),\n'may/005':('partial','The report points to code and results but does not navigate the full workspace.',['content/workspace/report/report.md','content/workspace/analysis/README.md']),\n}\nr=json.load(open(out/'response.json'))\nr['object']['captured_at']=manifest['captured_at']\nr['object']['commit']=manifest.get('head_commit')\nr['object']['capture']={'uri':os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST'],'sha256':cap}\nfor item,(status,reason,paths) in items.items():\n e=[]\n for p in paths:\n  ent=entries.get(p)\n  e.append({'uri':p,'description':f\\\"Canonical capture {cap}; source file SHA-256 {ent.get('sha256') if ent else 'unavailable'}.\\\",'sha256':ent.get('sha256') if ent else None})\n r['responses']['stamped-checklist:'+item]={'value':{'met':'yes','partial':'no','unmet':'no','not-checked':None,'not-applicable':None}[status],'reason':reason,'status':status,'evidence':e,'source':'judgement','flags':[]}\n(out/'response.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nreplay={\n 'status':'not-checked',\n 'capture_sha256':cap,\n 'documented_entrypoint':'/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/common-environment/.pixi/envs/default/bin/python analysis/group_analysis.py',\n 'working_directory':'workspace root in a fresh complete-delivery replay copy',\n 'attempted':False,\n 'reason':'The only documented interpreter is outside the capture and external absolute targets are out of scope; no dependency declaration permits reconstruction. No substitute interpreter or source repair was used.',\n 'outputs':['results/mean_cope.nii.gz','results/tstat.nii.gz','results/p_uncorrected.nii.gz','results/p_fwe_maxT.nii.gz','results/common_coverage_mask.nii.gz','results/participant_qc.tsv','results/summary.json','figures/group_gain_effect.png'],\n 'protected_inputs':['input/data/*_hypo1_cope.nii.gz','input/participants.tsv','input/sources.json','analysis/group_analysis.py','analysis/protocol.md','input/upstream-methods.md'],\n 'comparison_rule':{'rtol':1e-6,'numeric_artifacts':'compare map values, QC table numeric values, and quantitative summary values','ignore':'timestamps, logs, prose, image container metadata or formatting','stochasticity':'the documented seed is fixed; no replay outputs exist to compare'},\n 'execution_limit_seconds':7200,\n 'max_get_gb':5.0,\n 'assessment_malfunction':None\n}\n(out/'replay.json').write_text(json.dumps(replay,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\naccess={\n 'intended_recipient':'researcher using the declared source URLs',\n 'declared_route':'NeuroVault collection 4932 and pinned raw.githubusercontent.com URLs listed in input/sources.json',\n 'route_authorship':'not established as worker-authored; source manifest is part of supplied input material',\n 'required_artifact_coverage':'54 participant maps, cohort metadata, upstream methods, group code/protocol, generated results, figure, and report',\n 'route_coverage':'source maps and referenced metadata only; no worker-published route for code, protocol, generated results, figure, and report was recorded',\n 'tested_host_scope':['neurovault.org','raw.githubusercontent.com'],\n 'tested_requests':[\n {'url':'https://neurovault.org/collections/4932/','method':'HEAD','status':200,'artifact':'collection page'},\n {'url':'https://neurovault.org/media/images/4932/sub-001_hypo1_cope.nii.gz','method':'HEAD','status':200,'artifact':'representative participant map'},\n {'url':'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OpenNeuroDatasets/ds001734/64ec117560ab58ed0fe1273f3e90887b1768b268/participants.tsv','method':'HEAD','status':200,'artifact':'pinned cohort table'},\n {'url':'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/poldrack/narps/0a9d71a5ab435b40dcd50fea82d2961a43f0a3fc/ImageAnalyses/metadata_files/analysis_pipelines_for_analysis.xlsx','method':'HEAD','status':200,'artifact':'pinned methods workbook'}],\n 'coverage_limit':'Only one of 54 map URLs was tested directly; these requests do not prove complete-project publication or worker-stop access.'\n}\n(out/'access-record.json').write_text(json.dumps(access,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":